{"chapter": 3, "sha256": "6cf83d6184732e908ecce1481042e4fbf359d5267ec71e17ef34ecbca752d680", "voice": {"voice_id": "ppLqTilh7rH7fbUVlXsf", "name": "David - Documentary", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "voice_settings": {"stability": 0.55, "similarity_boost": 0.8, "style": 0.15, "use_speaker_boost": true}}, "source": "docs/script.md", "files": {"narration": {"file": "ch3.mp3", "text": "At the Sphinx's paws stand two temples. The Valley Temple is lined with red granite over a limestone core, in blocks that Flinders Petrie found ranging to over a hundred tons each. Those blocks were cut from the Sphinx's own ditch; all sides agree.\n\nJohn Anthony West and Schoch went further. In a 1993 film they said the limestone behind the granite is rounded and fissured like the ditch walls, and the granite was cut to fit it. Nobody weathers a wall and then cases it, they say: the granite is a refit.\n\nMark Lehner answers that the exposed cores weathered only after being cleared in the early 1900s.\n\nKhafre's statues, found inside, show he used the temple. They leave its core's age open.\n\nAnd Egypt's own records put long ages before its first king.", "seconds": 58.0, "alignment": {"characters": ["A", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "S", "p", "h", "i", "n", "x", "'", "s", " ", "p", "a", "w", "s", " ", "s", "t", "a", "n", "d", " ", "t", "w", "o", " ", "t", "e", "m", "p", "l", "e", "s", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "V", "a", "l", "l", "e", "y", " ", "T", "e", "m", "p", "l", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "l", "i", "n", "e", "d", " ", "w", "i", "t", "h", " ", "r", "e", "d", " ", "g", "r", "a", "n", "i", "t", "e", " ", "o", "v", "e", "r", " ", "a", " ", "l", "i", "m", "e", "s", "t", "o", "n", "e", " ", "c", "o", "r", "e", ",", " ", "i", "n", " ", "b", "l", "o", "c", "k", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "F", "l", "i", "n", "d", "e", "r", "s", " ", "P", "e", "t", "r", "i", "e", " ", "f", "o", "u", "n", "d", " ", "r", "a", "n", "g", "i", "n", "g", " ", "t", "o", " ", "o", "v", "e", 